# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# CREDENTIALS AND IMAGERY ACCESS - never commit anything matching these.
#
# This indicator reads an orthophoto that the user supplies. The imagery
# behind the published results is commercial, licensed data: neither it
# nor the access details may be redistributed, and nothing identifying a
# particular provider belongs in this repository.
#
# Configure your own source with $ORTHOPHOTO_SOURCE_PATH (and
# $ORTHOPHOTO_SOURCE_USERPWD if it needs authentication), or by copying
# orthophoto_access.template.txt to orthophoto_access.txt - the template
# is committed, the filled-in file is not.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
orthophoto_access.txt
Pass_URL*
*credential*
*password*
.env

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The canopy-height model itself. Apache-2.0 and freely available, but it
# is ~760 MB with the checkpoints and is upstream's to distribute, not
# ours. CHM_MODEL_SETUP.md documents cloning it and fetching the weights
# from Meta's public "Data for Good" bucket.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
chm_model/HighResCanopyHeight-main/
chm_model/__pycache__/
chm_model/*.pth
chm_model/*.ckpt
.venv_chm/
*.pyc

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large, re-fetchable or regenerable data. The per-polygon predictions in
# Data/OpenS_data/meta_chm_national_RAW_2026-09-17/ ARE committed - they
# are the reproducibility anchor and cost ~90 hours of compute.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Data/OpenS_data/nin_data/
Data/OpenS_data/bioclim/
Data/OpenS_data/eth_canopy_height/
Data/OpenS_data/*.gpkg
Data/OpenS_data/eth_canopy_height_national.csv

# Scratch from a national run (per-region tiles and predictions).
gjen002_national/
Data/OpenS_data/meta_chm_scratch/

# R / OS junk
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj
*.Rout
Rplots.pdf
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
